[CR CR0565r1 for 38.213] Reason for change: RAN1#114bis agreed that for a TDD RedCap UE, in a BWP with NCD-SSB, the slot determination for PUCCH repetition resource counting is based on CD-SSB. The RAN1 discussion is captured under Issue #2 in R1-2310324 from RAN1#114bis and under Issue #3 in R1-2312278 from RAN1#115. Summary of change: The definition of “SS/PBCH block symbol” is corrected so that it only considers CD-SSB, not NCD-SSB. Consequences if not approved: If the CR is not approved, the specification is not aligned with the above RAN1#114bis agreement and may give the impression that the slot determination is affected by the NCD-SSB configuration when it is not. However, since each NCD-SSB transmission is time aligned with a CD-SSB transmission in TDD according to another RAN1#114bis agreement (see Issue #3 in R1-2310324), this CR is not expected to change the UE behavior.
